# Cargo's build directory. Nothing in it is authored — fingerprints, object
# files, incremental state and dependency builds, all reproducible from the
# sources by `cargo build`.
#
# 402 of these were committed in "Initial project creation." and never
# touched again, which made build output 72% of the repository's tracked
# files and left ~2700 more of them untracked in every `git status`. They
# are ignored and untracked as of 2026-09-19; the files themselves stay on
# disk, and `git rm -r --cached target` is what took them out of the index.
/target

# The review loop's captured frames live under it, at target/review-frames/:
# the PNGs stage 5 looks at plus each frame's declared cell grid. Covered by
# the rule above, named here because `mjolnir-review` keeps only the last
# three runs and a reader looking for an older one should find out where it
# went.

# Written by Mjolnir itself: answering "for this project" at a permission
# prompt appends the grant here, so it's whatever this developer approved.
# The other .mjolnir/ files are hand-authored and stay tracked.
/.mjolnir/permissions.yaml
